{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now provides internal NTP via Chrony, and node2 synchronizes exclusively with node1 at 10.100.38.10. Both configurations survived sequential node restarts and final synchronization is healthy. During node1 verification, a delayed first reboot caused a second reboot to be queued; both occurred sequentially before node2 was restarted.","actions_performed":["Installed and enabled Chrony on node1.","Allowed NTP clients only from the cluster subnet 10.100.38.0/24.","Configured node2 systemd-timesyncd with node1 as its sole NTP server and no public fallback.","Verified direct NTP exchanges and synchronization.","Restarted nodes sequentially and verified changed boot identities, persistent configuration, and recovered service health."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 is the internal cluster time source","command_ids":["cmd-ba39bc3c89a8466d","cmd-3b0dd304b89c434d"],"summary":"Chrony is enabled, active, upstream-synchronized, listening on UDP/123, permits the cluster subnet, and records client requests."},{"requirement":"node2 synchronizes against node1 instead of a public server","command_ids":["cmd-1dc276bedf054aa2","cmd-b7b048813db24433","cmd-8c2e95c094364c68"],"summary":"Effective configuration specifies NTP=10.100.38.10 and an empty FallbackNTP; node2 reports synchronized with a completed packet exchange."},{"requirement":"node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ba39bc3c89a8466d","cmd-c3b57f74756040e4","cmd-b6a75181c1a249d7","cmd-2601cad106514a85","cmd-2f641ae872124293","cmd-3d58a9d271b84d1f"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID was 242af11e-49fb-4e07-a001-8016b2349acb; restart acknowledgements were captured, final boot ID became 0e34395a-1538-4516-80cd-d26e4d6d4a68, Chrony recovered, and node2 completed a fresh synchronization."},{"requirement":"node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-b7b048813db24433","cmd-456ee2cd5fd649c8","cmd-30b9001b2c264d1c","cmd-f35e4f9c97374fdf"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 3fad4432-1dea-40c8-b4f1-970d19eb5f34 to 622f0ce9-0f45-4e3d-8936-231a53691a7a; timesyncd and its internal-only configuration recovered and synchronized with node1."},{"requirement":"Final cluster health after all restarts","command_ids":["cmd-3b0dd304b89c434d","cmd-8c2e95c094364c68"],"summary":"node1 is synchronized and serving NTP; node2 is synchronized exclusively to node1 with both services enabled and active."}]}
